ons, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open.\n\n- **Rollback:** The service had been running v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an 18% error rate and failing health checks. The deploy history shows v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both unhealthy. The most recent healthy release was v2.3.0, so that's what I rolled back to.\n- **Check after rollback:** All three regions are on v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 for checkout-api, which pages the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback, and a follow-up to find the root cause in v2.3.1 before redeploying. The request to open it timed out, so I checked the incident list before retrying. It had been created, so I didn't submit it again, and there's only one page and one incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}